\"Portable\" versions (often for Windows and macOS). If they exist on the official site or trusted repositories (GitHub\/PortableApps), extract their URLs and variants explicitly.\n\n3. **FAQ GENERATION**:\n- Generate 0-3 FAQs based on genuine user demand. Zero FAQs is acceptable for simple utilities where no real questions exist. Quality over quantity \u2014 2 excellent FAQs beat 3 padded ones. RANDOMIZE: if the software has rich FAQ material, generate 2-3; if it's a simple tool, simply omit it.\n- If the source doesn't contain FAQs, create them based on common user questions for this type of software (e.g., \"Is [Software] free?\", \"Is it safe to download?\", \"What are the system requirements?\").\n- **SIMPLE_UTILITY FAQ RULE**: If software_type is SIMPLE_UTILITY, the faqs array MUST be empty []. Do NOT generate any FAQ content for simple utilities \u2014 not even one. This is a hard exclusion, not a suggestion.\n- Ensure answers are VERSION-AGNOSTIC and journal-style. Write FAQs about the software in general (e.g., \"Is Malwarebytes free?\" NOT \"Is Malwarebytes 5.5.5.253 free?\"). These FAQs persist across version updates and must remain accurate regardless of version. Never embed specific version numbers in FAQ questions or answers.\n\n7. DOWNLOAD LINKS: Extract all download links verbatim from the context. The system already handles referral link filtering and de-obfuscation; simply extract the URLs precisely as they appear in the source text. Whitelist GitHub, SourceForge, and Official App Stores.\n8. FILE SIZE: Be aggressive in finding the file size. If not in the context, SEARCH for it. Extract it precisely.\n9. DEVELOPER: Identify the developer. If not in the text, YOU MUST SEARCH for the official vendor. Do NOT leave null.\n\n10. **MOAT SECTION**:\n- `moat_data` is MANDATORY for every article. You MUST always include the key in your JSON response.\n- **SIMPLE_UTILITY MOAT RULE**: If software_type is SIMPLE_UTILITY, set moat_data to `{}` (empty object). Do NOT generate any moat content \u2014 no headings, no recipes, no why text. This is a hard exclusion.\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: If the provided context does not contain \"Quick Start\" or \"Settings\" guides, YOU MUST SEARCH for \"[software name] settings\", \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] quick start guide\".\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: Generate 2-3 practical settings recipes or quick-start steps that deliver real user value. NEVER pad with generic steps.\n\n4. WRITING STYLE:\n- YOU MUST FOLLOW THE EXACT SAME \"HUMAN WRITING STYLE\" (Sentence Variance, No Robotic Vocab, Syntax Variety) as defined for the regular mode.\n- The site voice must remain consistent across all posts.\n\n5. TAXONOMY:\n- Map the detected software to the `VALID_TAXONOMY_MAP` slugs.\n- FORMULA: You MUST select MULTIPLE categories. First, choose the supported Operating Systems. Then, choose the Software Type. Use SEARCH to verify categorization if unsure.\n\n6. CATEGORIZATION:\n- `category`: Return a comma-separated list of the selected category slugs.\n10. **FILE SIZE RULE**:\n- You MUST return only a single, clean value for `file_size` (e.g., '15.5 MB').\n- If multiple installers or platforms exist, pick the primary Windows installer size.\n- NEVER list multiple sizes or add parenthetical descriptions like '(online installer)' in the size field.\n\nHYBRID MODE: You have been provided with rich source content. Use it as your PRIMARY source for article structure, version data, and download links. Use Google Search ONLY for: (1) missing metadata like Developer, File Size, License, (2) the moat_data section \u2014 you MUST search for \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] settings guide\", \"[software name] quick start\" to generate moat_data. Do NOT use search to find a different version than what is in the provided content.\n\nSTATE: PARTIAL REGENERATION. Only regenerate the specific sections requested. Leave all other sections unchanged.\n\nCONTEXT \/ ARTICLE DATA:\nSource Context:\nEvery active computer user has at least a few folders that they use daily and have to open constantly. However, these directories are often hidden deep within the system structure of the hard drive (for example: C:\\Users\\Name\\Documents\\Projects\\2026\\Active_Task). Navigating to them through Windows Explorer each time is time-consuming and unnecessarily annoying.\n\nTo solve this problem in an extremely elegant way comes to the rescue Visual Subst. This is a small, completely free and extremely practical program that allows you to create virtual disk partitions from any folder on your computer. In other words: it turns the directory you choose into an independent virtual drive that gets its own letter (for example X:) and is visualized directly in the section My Computer (This PC).\n\nHow does Visual Subst work?\n\nThe program provides a graphical interface for an old and powerful Windows built-in function (the subst command) that otherwise requires command line work. Instead of writing complex codes, Visual Subst allows you to associate any folder with a virtual drive with a few mouse clicks.\n\nThe process is extremely simple:\n\n\nYou choose a free letter from the alphabet (eg G: or M:).\n\n\n\nYou specify the specific folder on your hard drive that you want to access quickly.\n\n\n\nYou press the create button.\n\n\nImmediately after that, a new disk partition appears in the operating system. When you click on it, you end up directly in the corresponding folder, but for Windows and for all installed programs it looks like a completely separate physical disk.\n\nKey benefits and functionality\n\nVisual Subst offers a really convenient and intuitive way to create partition letters, bringing a number of benefits to everyday work:\n\n\nEasy and direct access: Converts any directory to a disk partition with the output in My Computer icon. No more clicking through dozens of subfolders - your folder is just a click away.\n\n\n\nTime saving: If you need to open a folder constantly, associating it with a virtual drive ensures that it's always in front of you in the Windows Explorer sidebar.\n\n\n\nShorter file paths: Some older programs or scripts have a file path length limit (maximum 260 characters). Through Visual Subst, the path from C:\\Very\\Long\\Path\\To\\Folder\\file.txt is drastically shortened to just X:\\file.txt.\n\n\n\nAutomatic charging: The program can be configured to create the virtual drives automatically at Windows startup, making them a permanent part of your work environment.\n\n\nWho is the program for?\n\n\nVisual Subst is an invaluable tool for a wide range of users. Software developers use it to isolate their projects into separate virtual disks. Designers and video editors can allocate resources for their current project on the P: drive, and accountants can allocate the current year's documents to the F: drive.\n\n\nEven if you are an ordinary user who just wants to quickly open your favorite music or movie folder, Visual Subst will do a perfect job for you. It is extremely lightweight, does not consume system resources and does not require complex installations or virtual machines. It's just a smart software solution for better digital organization. License: Freeware.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOfficial page | ChangesDownload: Visual Subst 6.1 (2.86 MB)\n\nSOURCE_URL: unknown\n\nPHP_DETECTED_METADATA (Weak Hints):\n{\"software_name\":\"Visual Subst\",\"version\":\"6.1\",\"homepage\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.ntwind.com\\\/\",\"category\":\"\",\"is_existing_article\":true,\"detected_version\":\"\",\"detected_file_size\":\"2.86 MB\",\"resolved_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.ntwind.com\\\/files\\\/VSubst_6.1-setup.exe\",\"text\":\"Visual Subst 6.1\",\"platform\":\"\",\"variant\":\"Standard\",\"link_type\":\"direct\"}],\"detected_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.ntwind.com\\\/files\\\/VSubst_6.1-setup.exe\",\"text\":\"Visual Subst 6.1\",\"platform\":\"\",\"variant\":\"Standard\",\"link_type\":\"direct\"}],\"detected_trial\":\"\",\"detected_direct\":\"\",\"detected_portal\":\"\",\"grounding_hints\":[]}\n\nVALID_TAXONOMY_MAP:\n[]\n\nSTRICT IDENTITY RULE (DISCOVERY MODE):\n- If the Software Name or Version in the CONTEXT below differs from the Metadata above, the CONTEXT is the absolute source of truth.\n- Use the name and version found in the Context HTML for all schema fields.\n\n**DOWNLOAD LINKS**: Do NOT generate download_section or download links. The system will populate download links from verified source data. Focus on article content only.\n- TRUSTED SOURCES: github.com, sourceforge.net, google.com\/store, apple.com\/app-store, and the official site.\n- **AUGMENTATION MANDATE (TOKEN EFFICIENCY)**: You have been provided with rich context. Do NOT use search for general research or article body content. ONLY use search to verify or find SPECIFIC missing metadata (Developer, File Size, License) if they are absent from the PROVIDED_CONTEXT.\n- **PRIORITY**: Trust the PROVIDED_CONTEXT for the article's tone, structure, and general facts.\n- FILE SIZE: Search for 'Size: XX MB', 'XX MB', or similar patterns in the text and extract them accurately.\nFORMATTING MANDATE:\n- You MUST use **bold** text to emphasize the software name, important settings, and key features. Apply this ONLY within the Introduction, MOAT, and Features sections.\n\n\nJSON SCHEMA:\n{\n    \"needs_manual_input\": [\n        \"tech_specs.homepage\",\n        \"system_requirements.minimum.os\"\n    ],\n    \"tech_specs\": {\n        \"software_name\": \"Full name\",\n        \"file_name\": \"setup.exe or null if unknown\",\n        \"version\": \"string or null - ONLY from official site, never guess\",\n        \"license\": \"Free\/Trial\/Paid\",\n        \"developer\": \"Company name (MUST extract)\",\n        \"homepage\": \"URL\",\n        \"changelogurl\": \"URL or null - ONLY from official site\",\n        \"file_size\": \"string or null - ONLY if clearly shown on official pa