[2026-09-02 15:29:48] [INFO] DEBUG: Moat Data Structure {"moat":{"_note":"Generated based on WACUP's plug-in ecosystem, customization options, and configuration depth documented on the official site.","content":[{"heading":"Set Up Your First Playlist with Portable Paths","recipe":"1. Open WACUP and load your music folder via the Playlist editor\n2. Go to Preferences \u2192 Playlist \u2192 Advanced\n3. Enable the option to use relative paths (the default)\n4. Save your playlist to a folder inside your music library","why":"Relative paths keep playlists portable, so moving your music folder to another drive or machine won't break the links to your tracks."},{"heading":"Enable the Dual Big Clock Windows","recipe":"1. Download or copy the Big Clock plug-in DLL if not already present\n2. Rename a copy of gen_bigclock.dll to gen_bigclock2.dll inside the Plug-ins folder\n3. Restart WACUP so both plug-in instances register\n4. Launch each Big Clock window from the plug-in menu","why":"Displaying two clocks side by side lets you watch elapsed and remaining playlist time at a glance, which is handy for long mixes or streaming sessions."},{"heading":"Improve Streaming Reliability on Slow Connections","recipe":"1. Open Preferences \u2192 Network\/Streaming\n2. Increase the network timeout value to handle slower connections\n3. Apply the updated libcurl connection setup settings from the latest build\n4. Test playback with your preferred Icecast or FLAC stream","why":"Adjusted timeouts and connection handling reduce dropouts and buffering interruptions, which is critical if you stream from personal servers or low-bandwidth sources."}]}}
