[2026-09-02 17:56:33] [INFO] API Gateway RAW Request [prov_1779643665_n0pte]: {"model":"nvidia\/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a professional software documentation writer. Use web search to find accurate, up-to-date information about the software. You are a strict JSON content generator. Return ONLY one valid JSON object with no markdown formatting and no code fences. No commentary. If information is limited, return null for those fields. Do NOT guess or provide inaccurate data if it is not the requested field. OUTPUT LANGUAGE (STRICT): Write the ENTIRE article and all natural-language fields (title, meta_description, focus_keyword, introduction, features, whats_new, faqs, pros_cons, installation_guide, moat_data, competitors, tags) in ENGLISH ONLY. Even when the provided source CONTEXT is written in another language (e.g., Bulgarian), translate and rewrite it into fluent, natural English. Never mix languages and never echo the source language into the output. Keep factual proper nouns (software name, developer, URLs, file names, version numbers) verbatim."},{"role":"user","content":"You are a technical software auditor. Your task is to process technical context and reformat it into a structured schema.\nAccuracy is your ONLY metric, but COMPREHENSIVENESS is your goal.\n\nSTRICT DISCOVERY RULES:\n1. DATA PRIORITY:\n- The provided CONTEXT HTML \/ CHANGELOG is your Primary Source of Truth.\n- If the Software Name or Version in the Context HTML contradicts the Metadata, YOU MUST USE THE DATA FROM THE CONTEXT.\n\n2. **SEARCH MANDATE**:\n- You HAVE access to Google Search. If any technical metadata (License, Developer, File Size, Category) is missing or ambiguous in the CONTEXT, YOU MUST SEARCH FOR IT.\n- **THOROUGHNESS**: Do not stop at the first result. Verify the official developer site. Identify the correct license (Freeware, Open Source, Trial, etc.).\n- **PORTABLE VARIANT MANDATE**: You MUST check for the existence of \"Portable\" versions (often for Windows and macOS). If they exist on the official site or trusted repositories (GitHub\/PortableApps), extract their URLs and variants explicitly.\n\n3. **FAQ GENERATION**:\n- Generate 0-3 FAQs based on genuine user demand. Zero FAQs is acceptable for simple utilities where no real questions exist. Quality over quantity \u2014 2 excellent FAQs beat 3 padded ones. RANDOMIZE: if the software has rich FAQ material, generate 2-3; if it's a simple tool, simply omit it.\n- If the source doesn't contain FAQs, create them based on common user questions for this type of software (e.g., \"Is [Software] free?\", \"Is it safe to download?\", \"What are the system requirements?\").\n- **SIMPLE_UTILITY FAQ RULE**: If software_type is SIMPLE_UTILITY, the faqs array MUST be empty []. Do NOT generate any FAQ content for simple utilities \u2014 not even one. This is a hard exclusion, not a suggestion.\n- Ensure answers are VERSION-AGNOSTIC and journal-style. Write FAQs about the software in general (e.g., \"Is Malwarebytes free?\" NOT \"Is Malwarebytes 5.5.5.253 free?\"). These FAQs persist across version updates and must remain accurate regardless of version. Never embed specific version numbers in FAQ questions or answers.\n\n7. DOWNLOAD LINKS: Extract all download links verbatim from the context. The system already handles referral link filtering and de-obfuscation; simply extract the URLs precisely as they appear in the source text. Whitelist GitHub, SourceForge, and Official App Stores.\n8. FILE SIZE: Be aggressive in finding the file size. If not in the context, SEARCH for it. Extract it precisely.\n9. DEVELOPER: Identify the developer. If not in the text, YOU MUST SEARCH for the official vendor. Do NOT leave null.\n\n10. **MOAT SECTION**:\n- `moat_data` is MANDATORY for every article. You MUST always include the key in your JSON response.\n- **SIMPLE_UTILITY MOAT RULE**: If software_type is SIMPLE_UTILITY, set moat_data to `{}` (empty object). Do NOT generate any moat content \u2014 no headings, no recipes, no why text. This is a hard exclusion.\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: If the provided context does not contain \"Quick Start\" or \"Settings\" guides, YOU MUST SEARCH for \"[software name] settings\", \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] quick start guide\".\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: Generate 2-3 practical settings recipes or quick-start steps that deliver real user value. NEVER pad with generic steps.\n\n4. WRITING STYLE:\n- YOU MUST FOLLOW THE EXACT SAME \"HUMAN WRITING STYLE\" (Sentence Variance, No Robotic Vocab, Syntax Variety) as defined for the regular mode.\n- The site voice must remain consistent across all posts.\n\n5. TAXONOMY:\n- Map the detected software to the `VALID_TAXONOMY_MAP` slugs.\n- FORMULA: You MUST select MULTIPLE categories. First, choose the supported Operating Systems. Then, choose the Software Type. Use SEARCH to verify categorization if unsure.\n\n6. CATEGORIZATION:\n- `category`: Return a comma-separated list of the selected category slugs.\n10. **FILE SIZE RULE**:\n- You MUST return only a single, clean value for `file_size` (e.g., '15.5 MB').\n- If multiple installers or platforms exist, pick the primary Windows installer size.\n- NEVER list multiple sizes or add parenthetical descriptions like '(online installer)' in the size field.\n\nHYBRID MODE: You have been provided with rich source content. Use it as your PRIMARY source for article structure, version data, and download links. Use Google Search ONLY for: (1) missing metadata like Developer, File Size, License, (2) the moat_data section \u2014 you MUST search for \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] settings guide\", \"[software name] quick start\" to generate moat_data. Do NOT use search to find a different version than what is in the provided content.\n\nSTATE: PARTIAL REGENERATION. Only regenerate the specific sections requested. Leave all other sections unchanged.\n\nCONTEXT \/ ARTICLE DATA:\nSource Context:\nTaking screenshots is an invariable part of our daily lives \u2013 whether we're preparing technical documentation, writing a blog article, sharing important information with colleagues, or simply capturing an interesting moment from the web. Often, however, the standard operating system tool or common screen capture programs offer nothing more than a raw, unedited image. To make a screenshot look professional, we usually have to import it into heavy graphics editors, which takes valuable time and effort.\n\nThis is where WinSnap comes to the rescue - a small, extremely compact and convenient program that completely changes the rules of the game in this area. It combines powerful screen capture capabilities with advanced automatic image processing and editing tools, delivering results that look like they came straight out of Photoshop.\n\nFlexible shooting modes and shooting of non-standard shapes\n\nOne of WinSnap's greatest strengths is its extreme flexibility in capturing monitor content. The program is not limited to just capturing standard rectangular areas. It has several specialized modes of operation, fully tailored to the current needs of the user:\n\n\nIn full screen (Full Screen): Captures absolutely everything visible on your monitor.\n\n\n\nOnly a given program (Application): Captures the entire workspace of the specific open application, ignoring the rest of the background.\n\n\n\nThe currently active window (Active Window): Automatically focuses and captures the window you're currently working with.\n\n\n\nSpecified region (Region): It allows you to manually and with pixel precision define the boundaries of the area you want to preserve.\n\n\nIn addition to these classic options, WinSnap seamlessly handles one of the biggest challenges facing this type of software \u2013 capturing windows with non-standard shapes. The program is able to automatically recognize the specific rounded corners, smooth interface frames and transparent elements of modern operating systems. It removes the excess background around them, providing a perfectly cropped graphic image with a clean alpha channel for transparency.\n\nProfessional filters and real-time effects\n\nWhat makes WinSnap a simply brilliant program is the ability to instantly apply various visual effects to the captured parts of the screen. Instead of wasting time on additional retouching, you can set the software to process the photo as it is generated. The program offers effects that rival the capabilities of Photoshop in terms of quality:\n\nColoring effects\n\nUsing the built-in filters, you can radically change the style and focus of your screenshot. The program allows you to quickly convert the image into classic black and white, color it into a warm and aesthetic sepia (characteristic reddish brown tone) or completely invert the colors to achieve a more abstract visual effect.\n\nShadow effects\n\nAdding depth is key to making a clip art look realistic on the pages of a document or website. WinSnap offers a built-in feature for adding fully realistic, smooth shadows. You can choose whether the shadow surrounds your image partially or completely, with the software precisely calculating the softness and dispersion of light around the contours of the window.\n\nOther personalization tools\n\nTo give your screenshots a unique look or to protect your intellectual property, WinSnap allows you to automatically watermark each image. You can also add a sleek outer outline, as well as rotate the captured screenshot to a specific angle, giving it a more casual, dynamic and modern pose in the final layout.\n\nAutomation, variety of formats and high comfort\n\nWinSnap is designed with maximum productivity in mind. The program supports a wide variety of modern graphic formats, which ensures that your files will be fully compatible with any multimedia platform or text program. You can easily save the captured screenshots in the following formats: PNG, GIF, JPG, BMP and TIFF.\n\nThe process of exporting and sharing is also maximally simplified and automated. There is the extremely useful option to automatically save the files to a predefined folder on the hard disk, saving you the annoying pop-up of windows asking where to save the file every time you press the capture key. In addition, the software can directly send the finished screenshot to the Windows system clipboard or automatically attach it to an email message ready to be sent to your contacts.\n\nTo complete the user experience, the software features a highly intuitive and multilingual interface with full Unicode support. During operation, the program emits a clear and recognizable clicking sound when shooting, which serves as an excellent feedback to the user that the operation was successful.\n\nIn conclusion, whether you are a system administrator, software developer, web designer, blogger or just an enthusiast who needs to frequently capture what is happening on the screen, WinSnap is an indispensable ally. With its compact size, low consumption of computer resources and a rich palette of automated effects, this program successfully turns ordinary screen capture into a fast, professional and pleasant process. License: Paid (Shareware).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOfficial page | ChangesDownload: WinSnap 6.3.1 (3.61 MB)\n\nSOURCE_URL: unknown\n\nPHP_DETECTED_METADATA (Weak Hints):\n{\"software_name\":\"WinSnap\",\"version\":\"6.3.1\",\"homepage\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.ntwind.com\\\/software\\\/winsnap.html\",\"category\":\"\",\"is_existing_article\":true,\"detected_version\":\"6.3.1\",\"detected_file_size\":\"3.61 MB\",\"resolved_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.ntwind.com\\\/files\\\/WinSnap_6.3.1-setup.exe\",\"text\":\"WinSnap 6.3.1\",\"platform\":\"\",\"variant\":\"Standard\",\"link_type\":\"direct\"}],\"detected_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/www.ntwind.com\\\/files\\\/WinSnap_6.3.1-setup.exe\",\"text\":\"WinSnap 6.3.1\",\"platform\":\"\",\"variant\":\"Standard